# Go runtime

- Module: `qLLM`. Prefer `cmd/qllm` + `internal/...` until a stable public Go API exists.
- Pass `context.Context` everywhere connectors run; honor cancel on budget timeout.
- Validate IR/preset/catalog before planning; map failures to protocol error codes.
- Connectors return normalized tabular batches; do not leak driver-specific types across the facade.
- Apply `min(sourceTimeout, limits.maxSourceMs)` per source call.
- Do not pull unbounded tables to “emulate” unsupported ops — return `UNSUPPORTED`.
- Secrets only via env referenced by preset (`*Env` fields), never hardcode in repo.
- Tests: table-driven for IR validation; integration against compose DBs when the harness is up.
